## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates understanding of real-time blind source separation in challenging acoustic environments. Outdoor drone applications with moving sensors and wind noise test knowledge of online adaptation, computational efficiency under strict latency constraints, and robust source-tracking at the edge.

## Key Concepts

- **Online Convolutive ICA**: Real-time demixing using forgetting factors for adaptation, requiring careful balance between tracking speed and stability
- **Per-Bin ICA vs Joint Diagonalization**: Per-bin ICA offers lower complexity and faster convergence but risks cross-bin permutation ambiguity; joint diagonalization enforces consistent demixing matrices across bins at higher computational cost
- **Cross-Bin Permutation**: Resolved using inter-channel phase differences (IPD), amplitude envelope correlation across bins, or frequency-wise continuity scoring
- **Dynamic Source Count**: Detected via eigenvalue analysis of the spatial covariance matrix, monitoring eigenvalue gaps to distinguish active sources from noise
- **On-Device Evaluation**: Synthesized ground-truth using pre-recorded bird calls convolved with measured acoustic transfer functions and synthetic wind profiles, evaluated with SDR (Signal-to-Distortion Ratio) and SIR (Signal-to-Interference Ratio)

## Code Example

```javascript
class OnlineConvolutiveICA {
  constructor(numMics = 14, numSources = 3, windowSize = 1024, hopSize = 512) {
    this.numMics = numMics;
    this.numSources = numSources;
    this.windowSize = windowSize;
    this.hopSize = hopSize;
    this.forgettingFactor = 0.995;
    this.W = new Array(numSources).fill(null).map(() => 
      new Array(numMics).fill(null).map(() => 
        new ComplexArray(numMics)
      )
    );
    this.sourceCount = 0;
    this.permutationCache = new Map();
  }

  processFrame(x) {
    const X = stft(x, this.windowSize, this.hopSize);
    const numBins = X.length;
    const separated = new Array(numBins);

    for (let k = 0; k < numBins; k++) {
      const Xk = X[k];
      const Wk = this.initializeDemixerIfNeeded(k);

      const Yk = this.perBinICA(Xk, Wk);
      separated[k] = Yk;
      this.updateDemixer(Xk, Yk, k);
    }

    this.resolvePermutation(separated);
    this.detectSourceCount(X);

    return istft(separated, this.windowSize, this.hopSize);
  }

  perBinICA(Xk, Wk) {
    const whitened = this.whiten(Xk);
    const Y = matMul(Wk, whitened);
    return this.applyNonlinearity(Y);
  }

  resolvePermutation(separated) {
    for (let k = 1; k < separated.length; k++) {
      const score = this.computeEnvelopeCorrelation(
        separated[k-1], 
        separated[k]
      );
      if (score > 0.7) {
        this.alignPermutation(separated[k-1], separated[k]);
      }
    }
  }

  detectSourceCount(X) {
    const cov = this.computeSpatialCovariance(X);
    const eigenvalues = this.eigenDecompose(cov);
    const gaps = this.computeEigenvalueGaps(eigenvalues);
    this.sourceCount = this.estimateSourceCount(gaps);
  }

  computeMetrics(separated, groundTruth) {
    return {
      SDR: this.signalToDistortionRatio(separated, groundTruth),
      SIR: this.signalToInterferenceRatio(separated, groundTruth)
    };
  }
}
```

